<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Dervish State</h1><p class="st-meta">1896 CE – 1920 CE (approx.) · capital Taleh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Somali religious and military state led by Mohammed Abdullah Hassan, which fought Britain, Italy and Ethiopia for two decades.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</a>, a scholar of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salihiyya">Salihiyya</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> order, returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the mid-1890s and began preaching in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbera">Berbera</a> against British rule and Christian missions. Rejected by local elites, he moved inland, won over clans in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nugaal-valley">Nugaal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogaden">Ogaden</a>, and in 1899 declared a holy war, building a movement of followers called Dervishes (Darawiish).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Dervish State was a militant religious community under the sayyid's authority, with a council of leaders, armed horsemen and riflemen. Hassan was also a celebrated poet. It defeated several British expeditions, including at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dul-madoba">Dul Madoba</a> in 1913, and built stone forts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taleh">Taleh</a>. Its raids devastated rival clans, and famine and war killed many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1920 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> combined aircraft, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">Camel</a> Corps and local levies to destroy the forts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taleh">Taleh</a>. Hassan fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogaden">Ogaden</a> and died there later that year. Many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somalis</a> remember the Dervishes as early fighters for independence.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dervish-state.jpg" alt="Dervish State" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Taleh-based_Dervish_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1896 CE – 1920 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Taleh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Somali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/somalia">Somalia</a>, <a href="/countries/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dervish movement, Darawiish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=dervish-state" aria-label="Dervish State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6017 1836 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dervish State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6337 2092L6240 2044"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6240 2044h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6337 2092h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6337 2092h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Taleh. <a href="/atlas?year=1908&amp;focus=dervish-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

